# Orby black (`#080808`)

When the user asks for **black** (UI backgrounds, buttons on lime, marketing surfaces, tooltips, etc.), use the project black token — **not** `#000`, `#000000`, `rgb(0,0,0)`, or `#02030a`. For **studio viewport** background, use `--orby-studio-bg` / `STUDIO_BACKGROUND` (see `studio-bg-isolated.mdc`) — not `--orby-app-bg`.

## Tokens (prefer these)

| Layer | Use |
|-------|-----|
| CSS (UI) | `var(--orby-black)` or `var(--orby-app-bg)` (alias) |
| CSS (studio viewport) | `var(--orby-studio-bg)` — **not** `--orby-app-bg` |
| JS (UI) | `ORBY_BLACK` from `scripts/constants.js` (`'#080808'`) |
| JS (studio backdrop) | `STUDIO_BACKGROUND` — **not** `ORBY_BLACK` unless values must match |
| Themes | `--brand-text` is aliased to `--orby-black` (lime CTAs, dark UI chrome) |

Defined in `styles.css`:

```css
--orby-black: #080808;
--orby-app-bg: var(--orby-black);
--orby-studio-bg: #080808; /* viewport only — see studio-bg-isolated.mdc */
```

## Do

- New surfaces, defaults, fallbacks, and color-picker defaults → `#080808` / tokens above
- `color-mix(..., var(--orby-black))` instead of mixing with `#000`
- `theme-color`, histogram/tone-curve fills → `ORBY_BLACK` or UI CSS token
- Studio viewport canvas (`.viewport`, `#webgl`) → `--orby-studio-bg` only
- **21∶9 cinematic letterbox** mattes → pure `#000` / `--cinematic-letterbox-black` / `CINEMATIC_LETTERBOX_BLACK` (not brand black)

## Don't (unless user explicitly asks for pure black)

- `#000`, `#000000`, `black`, `#02030a` for brand/UI black
- Hardcoding gray `#888888` from an old mistake — that was wrong; brand black is `#080808`

## OK to leave as-is

- **Transparent shadows**: `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.x)` for overlays, scrims, box-shadow depth (not brand fill color)
- **Tinted panels**: `--panel`, `--panel-alt` (purple/blue UI chrome, not flat black)
- **Legal site** (`legal/legal.css`) unless the task touches it

When adding a new black default, update the token source only if the brand value changes — do not scatter new hex literals.
